  "name": "LITMO: LITerature-driven Modular Ontologies",
  "alternateName": "LITMO",
  "description": "An open-source web tool that builds modular OWL ontologies from a field's literature with a large language model as a drafting partner, following the Modular Ontology Modeling (MOMo) methodology. Papers are read one by one into a concept inventory with verified quotes; generation runs module by module and records the sources of every class; competency questions and hold-out questions from the literature run as SPARQL tests; a reasoner checks the result; the team decides at every step.",
